<title>USA: US hopeful on insurance talks with Japan.</title>
<headline>US hopeful on insurance talks with Japan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. trade negotiators are hopeful they can settle a dispute with Tokyo over deregulation of Japan's lucrative insurance market, a U.S. trade official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Senior U.S. Trade Representative negotiator Ira Shapiro and Eisuke Sakakibara, director general of the Ministry of Finance's International Finance Bureau, are scheduled to meet Tuesday and are expected to discuss a timetable for further negotiations on insurance, the official said.</p>
</text>
